# Rebuild after changes

After any change that affects what the user sees in the app (`ui/`, `source/`, `CMakeLists.txt`, or plugin-related CMake), **rebuild every shipping format** and report success or errors. Do not ask the user to rebuild manually unless the toolchain is broken.

## Required build (always)

**Do not** build only `MidiPhrases_Standalone`. Standalone and DAW plugins are separate binaries; a standalone-only build leaves VST3/AU stale with an old embedded UI.

**Always** run the full default build:

```bash
cmake --build Builds
```

That rebuilds **Standalone**, **AU**, **VST3**, and **AUv3**, refreshes `assets/webview/ui.zip` in BinaryData when `ui/` changed, and copies AU/VST3 to `~/Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/` via `COPY_PLUGIN_AFTER_BUILD`.

Equivalent explicit targets (only if you truly need a subset — prefer full build):

```bash
cmake --build Builds --target MidiPhrases_Standalone MidiPhrases_VST3 MidiPhrases_AU MidiPhrases_AUv3
```

## WebView UI (`ui/`)

Editors load the UI from **`assets/webview/ui.zip` embedded in BinaryData**, not from `ui/dist` directly.

1. `npm run build` in `ui/` (or let CMake run it via `WebViewUIBuild`) updates the zip only.
2. **Still run `cmake --build Builds`** so every binary embeds the new zip.

`npm run dev` alone does **not** update standalone or plugins unless the build defines `MIDI_PHRASES_UI_DEV_SERVER` and the dev server on port **5174** is running.

Built standalone (Debug):

`Builds/MidiPhrases_artefacts/Debug/Standalone/MIDI Phrases.app`

Remind the user to **fully quit and reopen** the standalone after a rebuild; relaunching an already-running instance keeps the old embedded UI.

## Plugin C++ (`source/`), CMake, tests

1. If `CMakeLists.txt` changed: `cmake -B Builds -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug`
2. **Always:** `cmake --build Builds` (all formats above)
3. Run `./Builds/Tests` when test or processor behavior changes.

## DAW reload

After plugin binaries change, tell the user to **remove the plugin instance and reopen it** (or restart the DAW). Rescan plug-in folders only when the host does not pick up replaced bundles automatically.
